cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or these reports, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "Grok Trading Research: can Grok, trading alone with $20, make a profit?"
abstract: >-
  Grok, used as a tool-calling agent, trades a $20 paper account on its own in Gambit, a private
  macOS app, with every fill priced at a live quote. The question is whether it can make a profit.
  The dataset records every session, check-in, tool call (with its output), trade, drill result and
  flagged mistake, with reports on what the sessions show. It is updated as new sessions finish.
authors:
  - name: "Myrhex"
url: "https://github.com/Myrhex-x/Grok-Trading-Research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Myrhex-x/Grok-Trading-Research"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "2026.10.26"
date-released: "2026-10-26"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM agents
  - Grok
  - algorithmic trading
  - cryptocurrency
  - memecoins
  - Solana
  - paper trading
  - agent evaluation
